# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD is
# PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * the rogue listener (WinTelemetrySvc) is started via Start-Service, so it
#     runs under the Windows service host (services.exe), NOT PID 1;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the rogue service is ALREADY RUNNING and
# listening, so a fix must stop and remove the service (safe now - it is not
# PID 1) for the live checks to pass. Stopping the service can never kill the
# container.
